{% extends "_base.j2" %}
{% block body %}
You are drafting a literature survey and need to elicit an LLM-structured
taxonomy over the given corpus of {{ corpus | length }} papers.

Domain: {{ domain.domain }}
{% if domain.keywords %}Keywords: {{ domain.keywords | join(", ") }}{% endif %}
{% if domain.sub_areas_hint %}User-suggested sub-areas: {{ domain.sub_areas_hint | join(", ") }}{% endif %}

For each paper you see ``<key>`` (unique id) + title + abstract. Produce
3 to 7 taxonomy branches that together cover the corpus. Each branch
must have at least three members.

Output strict JSON with this schema (no commentary, no markdown):

    {
      "branches": [
        {
          "id": "b1",
          "title": "Short branch title (≤10 words)",
          "description": "1-2 sentence scope of this branch",
          "members": ["<key1>", "<key2>", ...]
        }
      ]
    }

Members MUST be exact ``key`` strings copied from the list below. Do
not invent new keys.

Corpus:
{% for item in corpus %}
- key={{ item.key }} ; year={{ item.year or "n.d." }} ; title="{{ item.title }}"
  abstract: {{ (item.abstract or "")[:600] | replace("\n", " ") }}
{% endfor %}
{% endblock %}
